      "problem": "If $f(x)={3}^{2{x}^{2}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={3}^{u},\\,u=2{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={3}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={3}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3)\\cdot (4x) \\\\  & =4x\\cdot {3}^{u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3) \\\\  & =4x\\cdot {3}^{2{x}^{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
